# Keep the .vsix lean: ship only the bundled extension + metadata.
.vscode/**
.vscode-test/**
.claude/**
.git/**
src/**
test/**
out/**
docs/**
node_modules/**

# Screenshots are referenced by the README (the Marketplace rewrites the
# relative paths to repo raw URLs) — they don't need to ship inside the package.
# The extension icon (media/icon.png) is NOT excluded and still ships.
media/screenshots/**

# Source maps and build inputs
**/*.map
**/*.ts
esbuild.js
check-package.js
# One line per tsconfig, NOT a `tsconfig*.json` glob, so adding a project is a
# deliberate decision here rather than a silent inheritance. `tsconfig.unit.json`
# (CHANGELOG: the test/unit type-check gate, Session 173) shipped INSIDE the .vsix
# until `vsce package` was run and its file tree actually read — the release gate
# reports a clean exit either way.
tsconfig.json
tsconfig.test.json
tsconfig.unit.json
vitest.config.ts
.gitignore

# Methodology / project-management artifacts (not part of the extension)
SESSION_RUNNER.md
SAFEGUARDS.md
SESSION_NOTES.md
BOOTSTRAP.md
RECOMMENDED_SKILLS.md
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE_TEMPLATE.md
CONTEXT.md
CONTEXT_TEMPLATE.md
BACKLOG.md
CHANGELOG.md
ROADMAP.md
PROJECT_LEARNINGS.md
HANDOFFS.md
methodology_dashboard.py
dashboard.html
dashboard_history.jsonl
**/.DS_Store

# Prior sessions' scratch work — probe scripts, fixture trees and throwaway
# tsconfigs. UNTRACKED, and it shipped inside the .vsix from ~2026-07-21 until
# Session 174: 3043 of the artifact's 3085 files, 84.68 MB uncompressed, against
# a real extension of 42 files. `vsce package` exits 0 either way.
#
# ⚠ `scratchpad/` is deliberately NOT in `.gitignore` (decided, Session 174).
# The `?? scratchpad/` line in every Phase 0 `git status` is the only
# human-visible trace that ~97 MB of prior-session scratch lives in this repo,
# and it costs exactly one line because git collapses the directory — it masks
# no other stray file. Silencing it would buy cosmetic quiet at the price of the
# one signal, so the packaging risk is carried HERE and by `check-package.js`
# instead. Reversing that decision is a one-line change to `.gitignore`; the
# .vsix stays protected either way.
scratchpad/**
